# Files Cloudflare (wrangler deploy) should not upload from dist/, gitignore syntax.
# Unlike Netlify (and Cloudflare Pages), Workers static assets upload hidden files too. Local deploys
# would then publish whatever untracked dotfiles sit in public/: .DS_Store from the macOS Finder,
# editor files, an .env by mistake. Builds from a git checkout (Netlify, Workers Builds) don't have them.
# So: no hidden files or folders at any depth, except .well-known (security.txt, app links), the one
# standard public dot-folder.
.*
!.well-known
